#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# riemann_siegel_z

#% text
# `riemann_siegel_z(t)` gives the Riemann-Siegel Z function `exp(im*riemann_siegel_theta(t))*zeta(1/2 + im*t)`, real for real `t`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `abs(Z(t))` is `abs(zeta(1/2 + im*t))`, and the real zeros of `Z` are the zeros of `zeta` on the critical line (DLMF 25.10.1).

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
riemann_siegel_z(0)
#% output
#= zeta(1/2)

#% cell
riemann_siegel_z(10.0)
#% output
#= -1.5491945461810235

#% cell
riemann_siegel_z(20.0)
#% output
#= 1.1478424121851991

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The first zero of `zeta` on the critical line:

#% cell
find_root(riemann_siegel_z(t) == 0, [t, 14])
#% output
#= [t -> 14.134725141734691]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The modulus of `zeta` on the critical line:

#% cell
abs(riemann_siegel_z(17.0)) - abs(zeta(0.5 + 17.0*im))
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `riemann_siegel_theta`, `zeta`
